ovements.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In order to support the appropiation of the movements, the patient’s hand model and amount of virtual aid to translate movements can be directly modified on the program.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"50%\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:50%\"><!-- wp:image {\"lightbox\":{\"enabled\":true},\"id\":736,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"http://localhost:10003/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/aided_therapy_overview.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-736\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":737,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://localhost:10003/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/user_journey-1024x488.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-737\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Download the project report <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lZVF-pNJp9UdKqm_bFqzITGzQWtZg1NP/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">[here]</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size\">References:[1] V. S. Ramachandran, Eric L. Altschuler, The use of visual feedback, in particular mirror visual feedback, in restoring brain function, Brain, Volume 132, Issue 7, July 2009, Pages 1693–1710, https://doi.org/10.1093/brain/awp135[2] G.L. Moseley (2004) . Pain. Graded motor imagery is effective for long-standing complex regional pain syndrome: a randomised controlled trial.[4] W. Priganc Victoria, W. Stralka Susan (2011). JHT READ FOR CREDIT ARTICLE #190. Graded Motor Imagery.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->','Hand rehabilitation for chronic pain','','inherit','closed','closed','','735-revision-v1','','','2024-07-30 11:11:08','2024-07-30 09:11:08','',735,'http://localhost:10003/?p=741',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (742,1,'2024-07-30 11:11:26','2024-07-30 09:11:26','<!-- wp:group {\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"Heading\"},\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}}},\"className\":\"heading\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"contentSize\":\"30%\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group heading\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"center\",\"level\":1,\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\"}}}} -->\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">Hand rehabilitation for chronic pain<br></h1>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|10\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|10\",\"left\":\"0\",\"right\":\"0\"}},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"var:preset|color|contrast\"}}}},\"textColor\":\"contrast\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-contrast-color has-text-color has-link-color has-medium-font-size\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);padding-right:0;padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);padding-left:0\">VR interactive system that allows specialists to remotely follow chronic hand pain patients.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"Content\"},\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\",\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\"}}},\"className\":\"content\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"wideSize\":\"60%\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group content\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-right:0;padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-left:0\"><!-- wp:html -->\n<div style=\"padding:56.25% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/721492032?h=2ed6b811f0&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp&autoplay=1&muted=1&loop=1;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Hand rehabilitation Project\"></iframe></div><script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"center\",\"level\":3,\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\",\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\"}}}} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\"><strong>Research background</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\"}}}} -->\n<p style=\"padding-right:0;padding-left:0\">The project is based on an existing rehabilitation treatment for chronic pain and complex regional pain, in this method patients place the unaffected hand in front of a mirror where the reflection makes the illusion of normal hand movements on the affected hand.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"center\",\"level\":3,\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\",\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\"}}}} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\"><strong>Design challenge</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\"}}}} -->\n<p style=\"padding-right:0;padding-left:0\">How can we develop an environment for rehabilitation specialists to support and motivate patients with CPRS to reduce their pain sensation with the help of Mirror Visual Feedback?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"center\",\"level\":3,\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\",\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\"}}}} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\"><strong>Implementation</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"50%\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"blockGap\":\"0\",\"padding\":{\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|10\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|10\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);flex-basis:50%\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The final solution involves digital recognition of affected limbs program which translates the limited movements to virtual “healthy” movements.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In order to support the appropiation of the movements, the patient’s hand model and amount of virtual aid to translate movements can be directly modified on the program.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"50%\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:50%\"><!-- wp:image {\"lightbox\":{\"enabled\":true},\"id\":736,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"http://localhost:10003/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/aided_therapy_overview.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-736\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"default\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":737,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://localhost:10003/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/user_journey-1024x488.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-737\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Download the project report <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lZVF-pNJp9UdKqm_bFqzITGzQWtZg1NP/view\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">[here]</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"small\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size\">References:[1] V. S. Ramachandran, Eric L. Altschuler, The use of visual feedback, in particular mirror visual feedback, in restoring brain function, Brain, Volume 132, Issue 7, July 2009, Pages 1693–1710, https://doi.org/10.1093/brain/awp135[2] G.L. Moseley (2004) . Pain. Graded motor imagery is effective for long-standing complex regional pain syndrome: a randomised controlled trial.[4] W. Priganc Victoria, W. Stralka Susan (2011). JHT READ FOR CREDIT ARTICLE #190. Graded Motor Imagery.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->','Hand rehabilitation for chronic pain','','inherit','closed','closed','','735-revision-v1','','','2024-07-30 11:11:26','2024-07-30 09:11:26','',735,'http://localhost:10003/?p=742',0,'revision','',0);
